TIP:  There are some tricky bits with Mark’s fingerpicking overlaying the melody.  Just prior to entering the bridge on the “This is us . . .” Mark plays a quick (C)-(G) and then (A) with that (A) being the chord played on “us.”  

TIP:  Also notice many of the chords come in early, at the end of the preceding word.

TIP:  Mark’s long guitar solo is a repeat of two bars of (A), two bars of (D) which repeats prior to a (C)-(G)-(A) which repeats the whole sequence until a piano comes in and a fade.
     

